laurel 2770: camera step 1 on the Mi A3 (SM6125 CAMSS: CCI + VFE48/ISPIF/CSID v5.0, the sdm660 type): find the four cameras. Slots from the DT (laurel_sprout-trinket-camera.dtsi over trinket-camera-sensor-qrd.dtsi) and vendor camera_config.xml: 0 rear IMX586 (qtech/sunny) or IMX582, CCI M0, CSIPHY1; 1 depth GC2375H (qtech) or OV02A10 (sunny), M1, CSIPHY0; 2 front S5KGD1 (ofilm/sunny), M1, CSIPHY2; 3 ultrawide S5K4H7 (qtech/sunny), M1, CSIPHY2 (MIPI switch GPIO 114/115). Sensor facts (7-bit address, chip ID register/value, power-up/down order + delays) from the stock /vendor/lib/libmmcamera_laurus_*.so sensor_lib_t, read by scripts/laurel/camera-sensors.py (scripts/laurel/camera-inventory.sh -> out/laurel/camera/sensors.txt; no blob in git). Rails are GPIO-switched LDOs on the camera flex (rear VIO 49 VANA 15 VDIG 14 VAF 123; shared VANA 20; front VDIG 82; ultrawide VDIG 21) + PM6125 L12A 1.8 V (VREG VIO) through topaz_rpm_write. New bsd/dev/laurel_cam{,_hw,_cci}.c + laurel_cam{,_core}.h: camss_top GDSC (0x145607c), GCC camera AHB / camss top AHB / CCI AHB + core branches, CCI RCG 37.5 MHz (GPLL0 early / 16; 19.2 MHz TCXO fallback with the cci_v1 timing), every branch checked (CLK_OFF) before the CCI is touched; MCLK0-3 19.2 MHz from the TCXO (no PLL) on GPIO 34/35/36/44 (gpio 44: function 7); CCI pins 37-40 cci_i2c pull-up; CCI controller 0x5c0c000 polled (Linux i2c-qcom-cci.c register map and command words; trinket DT timings = cci_v2), NACK = ENXIO, errors halt + reset the master. Per slot: power-up list, chip ID of each candidate (16-bit big-endian, at most 400 kHz; OV02A10 100 kHz), power-down list, pins released (input, pull-down); then clocks, GDSC and the CCI RCG back as the boot left them, L12A off. Host test scripts/laurel/cam-test.sh (core header from this patch; cross-check with sensors.txt). One line 'LAUREL CAMERA: on: rear IMX586 (0x1a id 0x0586), depth GC2375H (0x17 id 0x2375), front S5KGD1 (0x2d id 0x0841), ultrawide S5K4H7 (0x10 id 0x487b); CCI 37500000 Hz, MCLK 19.2 MHz; capture path: step 2' (a slot without an answer: 'front: no answer (NACK at 0x2d)') or 'LAUREL CAMERA: off: <why>'; sysctl kern.laurel_camera = the same text. Kill switch camera=0. A failure turns off only the camera. No SPMI, TrustZone, SMMU or pool use in step 1. Step 2 (CSIPHY/CSID/ISPIF/VFE RDI raw frames into a pool buffer, sensor mode tables from the vendor libraries at run time) and the iOS side: docs/laurel_sprout/camera.md.

